{"title":"Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/d/dbdac26cf9468bfb738622d4083c4bb1625e8e3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + y^2 - 30x - 40y + 24^2 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"238\" height=\"18\" />, then the largest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/7/c471843498de1d9d0b05ad7f32eab45e216577b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{y}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"12\" height=\"33\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/b/53bf1afcb274a3bb84338109fffec8a1f1c02008.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><b>Solution 1</b>\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Completing_the_square\" title=\"Completing the square\">Completing the square</a> to find a geometric interpretation,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/3/a43036bd5906bfbcb5c0e4e2b548620a1c52b254.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + y^2 - 30x - 40y + 24^2 = 0 \\Longleftrightarrow (x - 15)^2 + (y - 20)^2 = 7^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"491\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Consider the line through the circle, passing through the origin, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8cab3b86d4a13c3cc3680c32aaa80cc854689e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = mx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"11\" />. We want to maximise <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/4/e74fb2bccc4561e615c2a75b287f7590e6a9f253.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{y}{x} = m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"54\" height=\"33\" />. If the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee61fd6e8a1926a802b97fc99b66b8687d8f620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"11\" height=\"15\" /> passes through the circle, then we can steepen the line until it is tangent.\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Pre2005_MockAIME_1-2.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/6/6c/Pre2005_MockAIME_1-2.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"264\" height=\"313\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Therefore we must find the slope of the tangent, when the following simultaneous equations has just one solution:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/5/18566482abcdfdebbb8e4c517a85dc199a79b3d1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{cases} y = mx \\\\ (x - 15)^2 + (y - 20)^2 = 7^2 \\end{cases}\\]\" width=\"217\" height=\"53\" />\nSubstituting,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/b/80bdd2226d893b09e9ddd7da542b86b182966e76.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x - 15)^2 + (mx - 20)^2 - 7^2 = 0\\]\" width=\"253\" height=\"19\" />\nIf there is one solution, the discriminant must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/6/3a695fa4bd5dd9fbefb0f984f387780efc0fd4ee.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[- 176m^2 + 600m - 351 = 0\\]\" width=\"211\" height=\"16\" /> \nSolving, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/6/dd6e3f5af7e837bb1994597de3c6ff6a4334448b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = \\frac {117}{44}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"69\" height=\"37\" /> (or the extraneous root, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6c7b3a87ac41dda30f661a9f5d2744ae46f3f39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" />). Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/3/e037ffcf8cfcbb8726182291567ff6c6c9b545a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + n = 117 + 44 = \\boxed{161}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"204\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p><b>Solution 2</b>\nWe obtain the previous circle as explained above. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> be the line that intersects the circle with largest slope. Draw the segment of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> from the center of the circle to the origin. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b1ac662f7ddbbce489953c8b7693848239564aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"14\" /> be the angle determined by the segment just drawn and the x-axis, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/1/2918f7d23f9ee8c04baabad86100d68023ec03f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> be the angle determined by the segment just drawn and the y-axis. \n</p><p>The slope of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/4/e6477295c0e966340e31e54c775144e1ea7f0cd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$tan (A+B)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />, or \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/1/e51fc8f91c6bf6c496ff5b3b03630b32057cc4ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {tan A + tan B}{1 - tan A tan B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"116\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>= <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/8/fb8fff1eb10edf50756e928b196633d7b72d9c46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {\\frac {4}{3} + \\frac {7}{24}}{1 - \\frac {4}{3} \\frac {7}{24}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"61\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p>= <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/f/e3fb46f762a180fe21ccd7ef27820812b95bad6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {117}{44}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"29\" height=\"37\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/6/6c6e74a6ef238d0df3b547558373f7ff5e191832.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {161}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005\">Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005 Problems\">Problems</a></b>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?t=14769\">Source</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017083029\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.041 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.083 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 209/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1422/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 180/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5002/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.892      1 Template:Mock_AIME_box\n100.00%   12.892      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6597:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017083029 and revision id 31352. Rendering was triggered because: page-vie